  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Undefined Behavior: What It Is and Why It Bites",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Undefined Behavior: What It Is and Why It Bites",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What UB Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Undefined behavior==: the standard sets **no requirements** on the program",
                "The compiler may ==assume UB never happens== and optimize on that",
                "UB is {red:not} a crash guarantee",
                "It can seem fine, fail only at `-O2`, or break after a compiler upgrade"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three Kinds of Unpredictable",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Kind",
                "Result",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Unspecified",
                  "one of several valid results",
                  "argument evaluation order"
                ],
                [
                  "Implementation-defined",
                  "valid, documented by compiler",
                  "`sizeof(int)`"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Undefined}",
                  "**no valid result**",
                  "`INT_MAX + 1`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. How the Optimizer Bites",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "int f(Node* p) {",
                "    if (p->x) return 1;   // p dereferenced",
                "    if (!p) return -1;    // check may be dropped",
                "    return 0;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "p was already dereferenced, so the compiler assumes p != nullptr"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "UB belongs to the ==whole execution==, not one line",
                "One bad **input path** poisons the entire run",
                "{red:Passing tests prove nothing}"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "UB has ==no valid result==. \"It works on my machine\" is not evidence of correctness."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Four Common UB Families",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Four Common UB Families",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Memory UB",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Out of bounds}: `a[n]` on `int a[n]` reads or writes past the end",
                "Even forming a pointer ==more than one past the end== is UB",
                "{orange:Use after free}, **double free**, returning a pointer to a local",
                "Freed memory may still look valid until it is ==reused=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Locals and `malloc` memory are ==indeterminate==",
                "`calloc` or `= {0}` initializes; `malloc` does **not**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Integer Overflow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Signed",
                "Unsigned"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`INT_MAX + 1`",
                  "{red:UB}",
                  "{green:wraps mod 2^N}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compiler may fold `x + 1 > x` to ==true=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Other Frequent UB",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Null== pointer dereference",
                "Shift by **>= width** or a negative amount",
                "Data race on a non-atomic variable",
                "Strict aliasing violation"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Looks fine, still UB",
              "text": "Dangling or uninitialized reads can ==work== in tests and fail later."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sanitizers: ASan, UBSan, TSan",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sanitizers: ASan, UBSan, TSan",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What They Do",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compiler ==instruments== the binary; the report comes at **runtime** with a stack trace",
                "Build with `-g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer` for readable traces"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which Sanitizer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Flag",
                "Catches",
                "Cost"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "ASan",
                  "`-fsanitize=address`",
                  "out-of-bounds, use-after-free, double free, leaks",
                  "~2x time, 2-3x memory"
                ],
                [
                  "UBSan",
                  "`-fsanitize=undefined`",
                  "signed overflow, bad shifts, null deref, misaligned",
                  "–"
                ],
                [
                  "TSan",
                  "`-fsanitize=thread`",
                  "data races",
                  "5-15x slower"
                ],
                [
                  "MSan",
                  "`-fsanitize=memory`",
                  "uninitialized reads (Clang only)",
                  "all code and libs instrumented"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Build and Run",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "g++ -g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer \\",
                "  -fsanitize=address,undefined \\",
                "  -fno-sanitize-recover=all prog.cpp"
              ],
              "note": "recover flag aborts on the first error"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ASan + UBSan: {green:one build}",
                "TSan: {red:separate build}",
                "Run the test suite and ==CI== under them"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never mix",
              "text": "TSan and ASan cannot share one binary."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not ASan with TSan?** Separate builds.",
                "**Abort on first UB?** `-fno-sanitize-recover=all`",
                "**Why MSan is hard?** Libraries need instrumenting too."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Valgrind, gdb and Core Dumps",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Valgrind, gdb and Core Dumps",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Valgrind memcheck",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==No recompile==; build with `-g` for line numbers",
                "Reports invalid reads/writes, uninitialized use, leaks; {red:10-50x} slower",
                "{red:definitely lost} = real leak; {green:still reachable} = usually fine",
                "`--track-origins=yes` shows where an uninitialized value came from"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "valgrind --leak-check=full --track-origins=yes ./prog"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Valgrind",
                "ASan"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Rebuild",
                  "**No**",
                  "Yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "slower",
                  "faster"
                ],
                [
                  "Stack/global overflow",
                  "missed",
                  "caught"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. gdb basics",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "gdb ./prog",
                "break file.c:42",
                "run",
                "next / step / continue",
                "bt",
                "frame N",
                "print var / info locals",
                "watch var"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Crash without a debugger",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "ulimit -c unlimited",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run, crash",
                    "sub": "core file",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "gdb ./prog core",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bt",
                    "sub": "backtrace",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Accurate values",
              "text": "Build with `-g` and ==-O0==; optimized builds hide variables."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Warnings as Errors and Static Analysis",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Warnings as Errors and Static Analysis",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Warning Flags",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Fail the build== on any warning, so warnings never accumulate"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Set",
                "Flags"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "GCC / Clang",
                  "`-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`"
                ],
                [
                  "MSVC",
                  "`/W4 /WX`"
                ],
                [
                  "Extras",
                  "`-Wshadow -Wconversion -Wsign-compare -Wnull-dereference -Wformat=2`"
                ],
                [
                  "Need `-O1` or higher",
                  "`-Wuninitialized -Wmaybe-uninitialized`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Static Analyzers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Find bugs ==without running== the code",
                "Static covers all paths; dynamic tools see only executed ones"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "clang-tidy file.cpp -- -std=c++20",
                "cppcheck --enable=all file.cpp",
                "gcc -fanalyzer file.c",
                "clang --analyze file.c"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Static",
                "Dynamic"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Paths",
                  "{green:All}",
                  "Only executed"
                ],
                [
                  "False positives",
                  "{red:Yes}",
                  "{green:None}"
                ],
                [
                  "Tools",
                  "clang-tidy, cppcheck",
                  "ASan, UBSan, Valgrind"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hiding a warning with a cast or `#pragma`, not fixing it",
                "`-Werror` on third-party headers: use `-isystem`",
                "Testing only debug builds: optimizer-exposed UB stays hidden"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Use both",
              "text": "Static analysis plus sanitizers or Valgrind. Each misses what the other catches."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Flags and Commands",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Flags and Commands",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Build Commands",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "g++ -g -O1 -fno-omit-frame-pointer -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined prog.cpp",
                "g++ -g -O1 -fsanitize=thread prog.cpp",
                "ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:halt_on_error=1 ./prog"
              ],
              "note": "debug build, thread build, runtime options"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "ASan + UBSan share ==one build==",
                "TSan is a ==separate build==: never combined with ASan",
                "Env options like `ASAN_OPTIONS` tune the run, no rebuild"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Valgrind and gdb",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "valgrind --leak-check=full --track-origins=yes --error-exitcode=1 ./prog",
                "gdb -ex run --args ./prog",
                "ulimit -c unlimited"
              ],
              "note": "after a crash: gdb ./prog core"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "gdb",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`bt`",
                  "backtrace"
                ],
                [
                  "`frame N`, `up`, `down`",
                  "move between frames"
                ],
                [
                  "`print x`, `info locals`",
                  "inspect values"
                ],
                [
                  "`break f`, `watch x`",
                  "stop at function / on change"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which Tool for Which Bug",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Bug",
                "Tool"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Out-of-bounds, use-after-free",
                  "{blue:ASan}"
                ],
                [
                  "Overflow, bad shifts",
                  "{green:UBSan}"
                ],
                [
                  "Data races",
                  "{red:TSan}"
                ],
                [
                  "Uninitialized reads",
                  "MSan or Valgrind"
                ],
                [
                  "Any crash",
                  "gdb backtrace"
                ],
                [
                  "Code smells",
                  "clang-tidy / cppcheck"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Sanitizers and Valgrind only see executed paths. Static tools see all paths but give false positives."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Compiled with -O2, what can `f(INT_MAX)` return, and why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Signed overflow is UB, so it may return 1 (folded to true) or 0 (wraps at -O0)",
                "Fix: check `x < INT_MAX` first, or use unsigned"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "int f(int x) { return x + 1 > x; }"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Two threads increment a plain int. Tests pass. Which build finds the bug, and can it share a binary with ASan?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "TSan (`-fsanitize=thread`) reports the data race",
                "No: TSan and ASan need separate builds"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Valgrind reports 'definitely lost: 40 bytes' and 'still reachable: 72 bytes'. Which one do you fix first?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Definitely lost: a real leak with no pointer left",
                "Still reachable is usually a global still held at exit"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}